        You will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. 
        Based on the commit message and modifications in the patch, you need to analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. 

        Here is the patch content:
        From b8e4e6c8866244fb5dd0d94b38d44fda8fd3ca68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry King <d.harry.king@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Feb 2020 10:22:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] JS: fix bug in parsing a number in the time formats
 'hh:mm:ss' and 'hh:mm:ss.ssssss'

Fixes bug introduced in c374ff3ebc6d11f67ac2ee1336f92a2fb96c6ff2
(JS: return simTime from 'parseRFC8601DateTime' instead of clock ticks)

Signed-off-by: Harry King <d.harry.king@gmail.com>
---
 src/main/java/com/jaamsim/input/Input.java | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/jaamsim/input/Input.java b/src/main/java/com/jaamsim/input/Input.java
index 614fdfe17..988ec072b 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/jaamsim/input/Input.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/jaamsim/input/Input.java
@@ -967,7 +967,7 @@ public abstract class Input<T> {
 			ret += hh * usPerHr;
 			ret += mm * usPerMin;
 			ret += ss * usPerSec;
-			return ret;
+			return ret * 1e-6;
 		}

 		if (isextendfull.matcher(input).matches()) {
@@ -995,7 +995,7 @@ public abstract class Input<T> {
 			ret += mm * usPerMin;
 			ret += ss * usPerSec;
 			ret += us;
-			return ret;
+			return ret * 1e-6;
 		}

 		throw new InputErrorException(INP_ERR_BADDATE, input);
-- 
2.25.1



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Root cause:<Root cause>

    You are a programming expert.
    You will be given the root cause of a bug and  the corresponding patch.
    You need to extract the code statements that lead to the bug from  the patch, based on the root cause.


    Provide a response strictly in the following format:
    Code statements:
    <text1>
    <text2>
    <text3>
    <text4>
    ...
    <textN>

Root cause:
ss.ssssss'. The original implementation returned the raw microsecond value, which was incorrect for the expected output format. The patch corrects this by multiplying the return value by 1e-6 to convert microseconds to seconds before returning it.
